cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SelectOmics: reproducible, leakage-proof feature selection for small-n, large-p classification"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Amanda S."
    family-names: Barnard
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4784-2382"
    affiliation: "School of Computing, Australian National University"
version: 0.7.1
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/amaxiom/SelectOmics"
url: "https://github.com/amaxiom/SelectOmics"
abstract: >-
  A feature-selection pipeline for classification in the small-n, large-p
  regime typical of omics. Features must survive three independent selection
  criteria, data cleaning, regularisation and wrapper methods, each decided by
  consensus across many independently seeded models, and each step reports the
  level of model agreement its panel actually holds at rather than one the user
  requested. A mandatory evaluation re-validates every step's panel and
  recommends one, and the held-out test set is touched once, on that panel, so
  the reported performance comes from samples no part of the selection has
  seen. On a pre-registered benchmark it returns short panels at a precision of
  0.970 and few false positives on data with no signal, at the cost of recall
  and runtime.
keywords:
  - feature selection
  - omics
  - biomarker discovery
  - consensus
  - high-dimensional data
  - machine learning
  - scikit-learn
  - Python
